  "text": "Virtualization lets software present and manage logical computing environments on physical resources. In a virtual machine example, a hypervisor manages the guest systems and their access to the host hardware. Containers provide another arrangement. They share the kernel of their host operating environment. The animation traces a virtual machine's physical dependency. More activity in an application can create more demand on processors, memory, storage, and networks with consequences for electricity and heat. Abstraction makes resources easier to use and manage. It doesn't remove their physical limits.",
